35,2,1,talk,Misaki,,Nine complaints died out because no one owned them. That silence is dangerous.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,The minutes show the same flats kept the covered spots for five years. No one ever reviewed it.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,The ledger is empty. No capital funds exist. Any new racks mean a direct levy on us.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,George,,"Twenty seconds per bike, plus greasing twice a year. That is a recurring physical burden, not a one-time fix.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Mio,,"The sticker register shows some flats have three bikes, yet they claim equal rights. That’s the real unfairness I’ve been sensing.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Mio, three bikes per flat? That explains the shifting. We need a cap to stop the morning chaos.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Mio, that is quite a lot. I wonder if the older residents are struggling to move that many bikes each morning.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"@George, twenty seconds sounds trivial, but the ledger shows zero maintenance budget. Who is actually paying for that greasing?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,George,,"@May, the greasing is cheap, but the lifting is the real strain. I need to know if we can share that load fairly.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, a cap makes sense, but I need to know if the daily riders actually agree to it before we enforce it.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Mio, I watched the exits. Four times, someone had to shift a bike just to leave. A cap prevents that bottleneck.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Misaki, that sounds exhausting. I worry about the older residents getting stuck in that shuffle.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,"@Shizue, the handover file shows three hours a month just reconciling cash. Adding per-place billing doubles that. Who is volunteering for the extra admin?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,George,,"@May, three hours is a lot. I am willing to take the physical greasing, but I cannot do the bookkeeping.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@May, I can help with the sticker checks! It’s simple, and I’d rather do that than the heavy lifting.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Misaki,,I am leaning toward a simple cap. It stops the shifting without creating a new bureaucracy that breeds resentment.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"I agree. A gentle cap would help, but we must ensure the covered spots are shared fairly, not just held by the same few.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,May,,I’m leaning toward a flat levy. It’s simpler than per-place billing and avoids the extra three hours of admin work.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,George,,"I support the flat levy. It keeps the admin light. I will handle the physical maintenance, but I need a clear rotation for the lifting.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Mio,,"I support the flat levy too! It’s simple, and I can handle the sticker checks to keep things fair.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
