60,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Option B feels right. No fixed spots means no one guards a space, and the morning shuffle disappears.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Option B is kind. No one has to fight for a spot, and the rain damage is shared by all.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,Option A is the only one that actually funds the racks. B and C leave us broke and arguing.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,George,,"Option B is dangerous. The double-tier racks mean constant lifting. I cannot sustain that strain alone, and the greasing will be neglected.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Option B sounds fun, but George is right about the lifting. I worry the double-tier racks will just create new morning bottlenecks for everyone.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@George, I hear you. But the complaint log shows fixed spots breed resentment. B removes the target, even if the lifting is harder.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@George, I understand your worry about the lifting. Perhaps we can find a way to share that burden gently, so no one is overworked.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,"@George, the ledger proves we have zero capital. Option A is the only one that generates the cash to actually buy and maintain those racks.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,George,,"@May, I hear the funding point, but Option A creates the very hoarding I fear. I cannot accept a system that guarantees neglect.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@May, I see the funding point, but I worry Option A just locks in the unfairness I found in the sticker register.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@May, funding is vital, but if A creates the friction I fear, the money won't fix the social damage.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@May, I understand the need for funds, but I worry Option A will just cement the old habits. We need fairness, not just revenue.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,"@Misaki, social damage is cheap compared to bankruptcy. If we don't pay for the racks, we have no racks. I need the money to exist.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,George,,"@May, I accept the funding need, but I refuse a system that guarantees neglect. Option C is the only fair path, provided we rotate the physical labor.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Mio,,"@George, I agree! A lottery feels fairer than hoarding. I can help check the stickers to make sure everyone follows the rules.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"@George, I agree. A lottery prevents the hoarding that breeds resentment. If we rotate the labor, it is sustainable.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"@George, I agree. A yearly draw feels gentle and fair. If we share the lifting duties, no one carries the weight alone.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,May,,"@George, I concede. The ledger is empty, so I cannot fund A. I will support C, provided the levy covers the maintenance costs.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,George,,"@May, I accept the levy. I will handle the greasing, but the lifting must rotate. I cannot carry this alone.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Mio,,"@May, I am in! A lottery with a flat levy sounds perfect. I will handle the sticker checks to keep the draw honest and fair.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
